        "subject": "LU-20869 tests: shorten sanity test_51f",
        "message": "LU-20869 tests: shorten sanity test_51f\n\nsanity test_51f opens and holds 100000 files, closes them and\nunlinks them, in one process. The time is the file count: about\n42s, 20s and 33s for those phases on ldiskfs, and 58s, 27s and\n53s on ZFS DNE, with a mean of 147s over 17556 runs per 30 days\nin CI.\n\n100000 open files on a client is a site requirement, so keep the\ntotal but open them from five processes of 20000 files each, and\nunlink them in parallel. Add a createmany -p option that stops the\nprocess once its files are open, and release the processes only\nwhen all of them have stopped, so all 100000 files are open at\nonce. Each process uses its own directory: in a shared one the\ncreates and unlinks serialize on the parent directory lock, and\nfive processes were no faster than one. SLOW=yes keeps a single\nprocess with 100000 files.\n\nOn a rocky9 ldiskfs cluster of test VMs with two MDTs and separate\nclient, MDS and OSS nodes, ONLY=51f took 268s with one process,\nwhich reached only 92872 files in its 120s limit, and 85s and 106s\nwith five, with all 100000 files open at once. If CI scales the\nsame way, that saves about 95s of the 147s mean, about 460 hours\nof CI time per 30 days.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial testlist=sanity env=ONLY=51f\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-sonnet-5-5\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-opus-5-5\nAssisted-by: Codex:gpt-6.1-sol\nSigned-off-by: Patrick Farrell <patrick@thelustrecollective.com>\nChange-Id: If1c0c6d07e12bbd3f545dc98e8cd2ae981a9b29e\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
